# shell: desktop
# PVS-045: icons dropped on the background of an icon-mode window land at
# the drop point KEEPING their arrangement -- what was picked up is what is
# put down, in the same shape.  Nothing consumed a landing position before:
# dropped icons were auto-placed at the top-left whatever the drop point.
key 1 ctrl
wait 6
note open sub and drag its window clear of the one it came from
click 102 119
wait 2
click 102 119
wait 8
key 1 ctrl
wait 6
drag-window /sub 620 420
wait 6
note two icons, a grid step apart, dropped at 600,500
click 221 119
wait 2
click 341 119 1 ctrl
wait 2
press 221 119
move 300 200
move 600 500
release 600 500
wait 20
click 580 414
wait 5
expect-rows 2
note the first lands under the pointer and the second keeps its offset
expect-icon-screen a.txt 600 500
expect-icon-screen b.txt 720 500
quit
